/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:136:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:137:Draw a polyline by decoding 3x3 glyph instructions read across a divided grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:138:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:139:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:140:- Left of a full-height vertical divider: 3x3 colored glyphs on bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:141:- Right of divider: a single gray (5) start pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:142:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:143:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:144:- Remove the divider; shift the gray start into the left canvas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:145:- Read glyphs in column-major order (left→right, top→bottom).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:146:- Each glyph's shape (pixel area) encodes a segment: area 4 → down 2, area 5 → right 3, area 6 → left 4, area 7 → left 2.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:147:- Append segments sequentially, stepping down one cell between each.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:148:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:149:Key insight: Glyph pixel count (area) uniquely determines both segment length and direction — the shape itself is the instruction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:150:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:151:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:152:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:153:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="eval" puzzle_id="3e6067c3" lines="7-20">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:154:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:155:Connect framed squares via colored bridges following a control-pixel sequence.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:156:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:157:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:158:- bg = background. Border color forms equal-sized framed squares with unique inner fill colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:159:- Control row below squares: colored pixels read left-to-right encode visitation order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:160:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:161:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:162:- Start at the square matching first control color c0.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:163:- For each consecutive pair (ci, ci+1), find the ci+1-colored square aligned in the same row or column band, preferring nearest.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:164:- Draw a bridge colored ci between the pair, spanning the gap with inner-square thickness.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:165:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:166:Key insight: Row/column-band alignment plus proximity resolves ambiguity when inner colors repeat.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:167:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:168:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:169:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:170:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="eval" puzzle_id="446ef5d2" lines="8-20">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:171:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:172:Assemble scattered rectangular pieces into a rectangle at an L-marker corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:173:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:174:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:175:- bg = most common color. Non-bg rectangular pieces scattered on the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:176:- 3-pixel L-marker (2x2 minus one cell) tags the corner; the gap is the corner cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:177:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:178:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:179:- rect_col = most common color across all piece pixels; all outer rectangle edges must be rect_col.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:180:- Translate pieces (no rotation) to tile the rectangle; touching edges must match, with rect_col as wildcard.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:181:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:182:Key insight: rect_col acts as wildcard during edge matching — only non-rect_col pixels at shared boundaries must agree.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:183:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:184:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:185:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:186:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="eval" puzzle_id="8698868d" lines="9-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:187:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:188:Match sprites to frames by connected-hole count, then nest each sprite inside its frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:189:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:190:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:191:- bg = azure (8). Large hollow squares (frames) arranged in a grid; smaller filled squares (sprites) placed elsewhere.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:192:- Each frame and sprite has a distinct color. Sprites may contain holes (non-sprite-color pixels).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:193:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:194:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:195:- Frames form a regular grid; some may be bg-colored (invisible).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:196:- Count connected hole regions inside each frame's interior and each sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:197:- Pair each frame with the sprite sharing the same hole count.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:198:- Place the matched sprite inside the frame border; recolor sprite holes to the frame's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:199:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:200:Key insight: The matching key is the number of connected hole components, not hole area or color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:201:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:202:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:203:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:204:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="eval" puzzle_id="e8686506" lines="172-185">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:205:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:206:Assemble scattered colored fragments into a left-right symmetric rectangle, jigsaw-style.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:207:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:208:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:209:- bg = most common color; remaining colors form small sprite fragments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:210:- Optional roles: 4 singleton pixels of one color mark corners; horizontal bars mark top/bottom edges; paired vertical lines mark left/right edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:211:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:212:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:213:- Collect all non-bg connected components as jigsaw pieces.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:214:- Determine output rectangle dimensions from total piece area.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:215:- Pack pieces into the rectangle so it is exactly mirror-symmetric (left-right) and same-color pieces never 4-touch.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:216:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:217:Key insight: Left-right symmetry plus the no-same-color-touching constraint make the assembly unique; corner/edge markers anchor it when present.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:218:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:219:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:220:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:221:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="eval" puzzle_id="db695cfb" lines="8-19">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:222:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:223:Connect same-color diagonal pixel pairs, then emit perpendicular rays from differently-colored pixels on those diagonals.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:224:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:225:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:226:- bg = most common color. Line color (e.g. blue) has pixel pairs aligned on shared diagonals. Trigger color (e.g. magenta) pixels sit along those diagonals.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:227:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:228:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:229:- Draw diagonal lines connecting each pair of same-color aligned pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:230:- Where the diagonal crosses a trigger pixel, emit perpendicular diagonal rays (in the trigger's color) extending to the grid boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:231:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:232:Key insight: Trigger pixels act as beam-splitters — the perpendicular rays rotate 90° from the connecting diagonal's orientation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:233:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:234:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:235:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:236:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="45a5af55" lines="5-18">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:237:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:238:Build nested square frames from a stack of horizontal color stripes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:239:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:240:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:241:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:242:- Each stripe has uniform color and variable height (1-4 rows).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:243:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:244:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:245:- Read stripes bottom to top.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:246:- Bottom stripe becomes the center solid square with side length = stripe height.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:247:- Each subsequent stripe wraps the current shape with a square frame of thickness = stripe height, in that stripe's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:248:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:249:Key insight: Stripe height doubles as both frame thickness and (for the innermost) center-square side length; output dimensions are fully determined by the stripe heights.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:250:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:251:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:252:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:253:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="eval" puzzle_id="b5ca7ac4" lines="7-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:254:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:255:Move bordered 5×5 squares to their designated grid edges by border color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:256:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:257:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:258:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:259:- Azure (8) and red (2) bordered 5×5 squares with colored interiors, scattered across the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:260:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:261:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:262:- Azure squares → left edge (col 0); red squares → right edge (col W−5).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:263:- Each square keeps its original row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:264:- Process azure left-to-right, red right-to-left (nearest-to-edge first).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:265:- If a square's rows overlap an already-placed edge square, place it one square-width inward instead.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:266:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:267:Key insight: Near-edge-first ordering plus row-overlap determines which square sits at the edge vs. the second column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:268:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:269:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:270:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:271:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="eval" puzzle_id="dfadab01" lines="79-93">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:272:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:273:Expand each colored control pixel into its corresponding fixed 4x4 glyph.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:274:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:275:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:276:- Black background with single-pixel markers in colors 2, 3, 5, and/or 8.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:277:- Some inputs also show a sample 4x4 glyph in the output color, with a same-rule marker just below-right of the sample.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:278:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:279:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:280:- Replace each marker color by its learned 4x4 glyph: 2->yellow frame, 3->blue ring, 5->pink diagonal blocks, 8->orange X.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:281:- Paint each glyph with its top-left corner at the marker pixel, clipping at the grid boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:282:- Remove the sample glyphs and skip their below-right label markers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:283:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:284:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:285:- The colored pixels are control pixels for a fixed glyph alphabet; non-control sample glyphs are only legend entries, not preserved scene objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:286:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:287:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:288:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:289:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="eval" puzzle_id="7b80bb43" lines="8-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:290:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:291:Remove diagonal staircase noise and complete broken straight lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:292:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:293:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:294:- bg = background; one foreground color fg forming axis-aligned lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:295:- Some fg pixels form 45° diagonal chains (8-connected but 4-disconnected from lines).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:296:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:297:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:298:- Delete all diagonal-only fg pixels (those with no orthogonal fg neighbor, only diagonal ones).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:299:- Fill short gaps in horizontal/vertical lines where a deleted diagonal was nearby.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:300:- Prune remaining diagonal-adjacent leaf pixels near former diagonal sites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:301:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:302:Key insight: Diagonal pixels are hints marking where a straight line is broken; their span sets the maximum gap size to fill.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:303:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:304:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:305:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:306:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="eval" puzzle_id="8b9c3697" lines="9-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:307:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:308:Insert red components into interior sockets of large structures, leaving a black trail.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:309:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:310:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:311:- bg = most common. Large non-bg, non-red structures with interior cavities.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:312:- Red components outside structures.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:313:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:314:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:315:- Interior sockets: bg cells inside a structure's bbox, adjacent to structure pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:316:- For each structure, find the direction where rays from sockets hit a red component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:317:- Slide that component into the socket; paint traversed cells black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:318:- Unmatched reds vanish.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:319:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:320:Key insight: Docking direction is inferred by ray-casting from interior sockets to the nearest red component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:321:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:322:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:323:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:324:<reference_puzzle index="19" source="eval" puzzle_id="f931b4a8" lines="10-27">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:325:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:326:Count the two upper quadrant control regions to size an output made from the lower quadrant pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:327:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed401141254/4/prompt.md:328:Input structure:
